# Tailwind CSS

Style layout, spacing, color, type, and responsive behavior with Tailwind utility classes on the component.

- Do not add a new `*.module.css` file. Do not grow an existing CSS module for new UI.
- Keep `corePlugins.preflight` set to `false` in `tailwind.config.js`. Existing CSS modules stay until that screen is edited.
- When a screen is edited, put the new or changed styles in Tailwind classes on the TSX. Leave untouched screens on their current CSS.
- Mobile layout uses `max-[980px]:` for the header breakpoint already in the site. Phone layout under that uses `max-[720px]:` where the rest of the site already breaks.

```tsx
// Bad — new CSS module for a button row
import styles from "./row.module.css";

// Good
<div className="flex flex-wrap gap-2 max-[720px]:flex-col">
```
